# Performance ledger

No runtime exists yet, so this ledger contains no performance wins.

Every future entry MUST bind:

- implementation commit and dirty state;
- exact device/model/platform/accelerator generations;
- replay/corpus digest and workload distribution;
- baseline and candidate commands;
- semantic-equivalence evidence;
- latency/throughput/queue/energy/cost distributions;
- sample count, variance, and warm/cold state;
- changed operation-cost terms;
- retained benchmark artifacts;
- regressions and excluded conditions.

A lower wall-clock number without the same semantic work and output quality is not a win.


Operationalization requirements:
1. Treat machine registries/schemas as higher authority, but record and repair any disagreement rather than choosing convenient text.
2. Preserve stable identities, assumptions, alternatives, failure/unknown states, privacy/security limits, costs, qualification and claim boundaries.
3. Add deterministic source-digest and heading/row coverage checks with typed drift diagnostics and owner/repair guidance.
4. Update the bead and its dependent proof whenever the source is deliberately changed; generated prose must remain a mirror, not a parallel contract.

Why: the plan's quality objective has zero code: event-level AUPRC, recall at a false-alerts-per-property-day budget, calibration, time-to-detect, and not_observable accounting. Without it, detection quality is unknown, not just unproven, and no threshold or model change can be judged.

What: a deterministic evaluation harness in Rust (fss-reference or a new small crate). Inputs: (a) a labelled clip set with event intervals, zones and not_observable intervals; (b) the event candidates a pipeline run produced. It computes:
- event-level precision/recall, with an explicit interval-matching rule;
- AUPRC over score thresholds;
- recall at a declared false-alert budget;
- the time-to-detect distribution;
- a separate not_observable bucket that is never counted as a negative.
Output is a canonical report naming the exact pipeline, model and policy generations. Tests use hand-computed metrics on small synthetic label sets, including ties, empty sets, all-negative sets and coverage gaps.

Honesty: synthetic scenes validate the harness only. No quality claim until the real consented-corpus bead lands.
